  "title": "Two-phase repair: unchanged stock LEGACY loop, then a bottleneck-driven TNS-recovery phase with a hard post-stock WNS floor",
  "hypothesis": "Every in-loop change so far (iters 8, 9, 12) found large Ibex TNS gains from shared-cone/TNS-aware repair but perturbed the stock trajectory and lost WNS on AES/gcd/JPEG. Instead of modifying the greedy worst-path-first loop, run it unchanged, snapshot design WNS W*, then run a separate phase that ranks driver pins by the slack-weighted count of violating paths through them (top-N=400 paths) and trials stock generator moves on the top-K drivers under a journal, keeping a move only if design WNS >= W* (absolute, non-rolling) and measured design TNS improves by >= 0.5 ps. Rounds repeat with re-ranking until no move is kept, 5 rounds pass, or a move cap of max(30, 10% of stock moves) is hit. This makes final WNS >= stock by construction while harvesting shared-trunk TNS (e.g. the Ibex _26153_ fanout-943 trunk, the JPEG HA/FA drivers), and moves on shared drivers of the worst cone can also raise WNS.",
